<title>YEMEN: British trade minister visits Yemen.</title>
<headline>British trade minister visits Yemen.</headline>
<dateline>ADEN 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British trade minister Anthony Nelson and a delegation of about 50 businessmen arrived in Sanaa on Friday on a three-day visit to Yemen, state television said.</p>
<p>British Foreign Secretary Michael Rifkind visited Sanaa earlier this month and said Britain planned to boost its trade relations with the Arab country.</p>
<p>Yemen, an impoverished country of 16 million people, is a small oil producer. Its economy, hit by a brief civil war in 1994, is slowly improving under reforms agreed with the International Monetary Fund.</p>
